Feature Review — Team Page & Login Styling

Team Page Requirements

 Team name displayed clearly at top of page
 Member photo displayed at consistent size, placeholder avatar is not used because all images are available.
 Member name displayed clearly
 Member role displayed (PM, BA, UX, Dev 1, Dev 2)
 Short blurb displayed per member

Team Page Display Requirements
 Consistent layout used across all team members
 Page remains readable across common screen sizes
 Member photos use consistent dimensions
 Text overlap with other content is not immediately present
 Long text does not wrap appropriately

Login Page Scope

 Styling-only changes applied (layout, colours, typography, spacing, buttons)
 No changes made to authentication logic
 No changes made to login functionality
 No changes made to Firebase/authentication configuration
 No changes made to session behaviour
 No changes made to user permissions
 No changes made to existing login validation logic
 Existing login functionality confirmed to behave as before

Edge Cases

 No photo → placeholder/default does not display
 Long name → does not wrap/resize without overlap
 Long blurb → does not wrap across multiple lines without overlap
 Missing blurb → member card still displays correctly
 Tested across different screen sizes → readable and usable

Overall: Feature reviewed end-to-end against requirements and design. Majority of items pass.
